I'm interested in what the boundaries are, what is and
isn't a fair ascension.  It seems that folks think wizard
mode testing or explore mode is fine in that such work
counts as neither cheating nor being ascendible.  So
where would the boundary be between what is and what
isn't cheating when doing tests.  Clearly a game started
from scratch to perform a test isn't cheating so long as
you quit.  Or a game with no tests and one sequence of
execution isn't cheating so long as you either die or
ascend.

Consider that a wizard mode test will often involve many
wishes to acheive a similar context to the current game
to be able to test something.  Yet the same context can
be acheived by saving the current game, switching into
explore mode, and then quitting when the experiment is
done.

Let's say I wanted to test something like using a
polearm at Ludios against using melee at Ludios.  So
I start two completely regular games and run them
through roughly in parallel until both have finished
Ludios.  Without savescumming.  Both are valid games,
right?  Yet being experiments it's time to quit from
one or both?

Or I start up two wizard mode or explore mode games
and run them through Ludios using the alternate
weaponry, note the results, then quit both.  It's a
valid experiment, right?

Or I have one game with a character who's just found
Ludios.  The character goes back out the portal and
saves.  One experiment goes to explore mode, uses the
pole arm, notes the result and quits.  One experiment
goes to explore mode, uses the melee weapons, notes
the result and quits.  Then the real character resumes
where the game left off.  And from then on it is a
savescummed game because I didn't use wizard mode and
a flock of wishes to get an original character to
Ludios.



